==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|əʊsɪs}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|de|en}} {{term|Mitosis|lang=de}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|μίτος||thread|tr=mitos|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}} + {{term|-osis|lang=de}}, probably in reference to the thread-like [[chromatin]] seen during mitosis.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|mitoses}}

# {{context|cytology|lang=en}} The [[division]] of a cell [[nucleus]] in which the [[genome]] is copied and separated into two identical halves. It is normally followed by cell division.

====Synonyms====
* [[karyokinesis]]

====Meronyms====
* [[prophase]]
* [[metaphase]]
* [[anaphase]]
* [[telophase]]

====Derived terms====
* [[mitotic]]
* [[mitotically]]

====See also====
* [[meiosis]]

